[J3x](https://github.com/amj3x) joined OpenZeppelin as a security researcher, contributing to the security of the Ethereum ecosystem.

## study-together

We introduced study-together sessions, a new layer of collaboration between security researchers. We had two sessions in January:
- Study [yETH exploit](https://github.com/banteg/yeth-exploit/blob/main/report.pdf) , featuring [no_secrets](https://x.com/no___secrets___) from [Asymmetric Research](https://www.asymmetric.re/).  
- Study [Hotstuff contest](https://audits.sherlock.xyz/contests/1233) right after the contest ended, featuring [Al-Qa'qa'](https://x.com/Al_Qa_qa), from [Cyfrin](https://www.cyfrin.io/). Here's the [recording](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VBP3n7nxYhc).

## Algiers Meetup


We organized Algiers Meetup, with 30+ attendees, 2 sessions and great energy. The theme was about applied mathematics in subjects of interest for the community.

IRL, we had a whiteboard session presented by [Rezazi Mohamed Abdessamed](https://www.linkedin.com/in/rezazi-mohamed-abdessamed/) from [Nethermind](https://www.nethermind.io/). It was an introduction to zero knowledge proofs.

![algiers meetup](/assets/images/algiers-meetup.jpeg)

Online, we had [Youssef El Housni](https://www.linkedin.com/in/youssef-el-housni-412427108/) from [Consensys](https://consensys.io/). It was about his career development from Math Olympiad in high school, to their [research](https://yelhousni.github.io/#publications) in applied cryptography securing millions of dollars on the blockchain. Here's the [recording](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bhoqHfUXK8k)
 
We thank [Fentech](https://fentech.ai/) for sponsoring the meetup!   
